# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules for mart.gokez.com.
#
# Intentionally EMPTY of rules. Do not add the usual SPA catch-all:
#
#     /*    /index.html    200
#
# Cloudflare Pages already provides SPA fallback natively. From the Pages
# "Serving Pages" documentation: "If your project does not include a top-level
# 404.html file, Pages assumes that you are deploying a single-page application...
# matches all incoming paths to the root (/), allowing you to capture URLs like
# /about or /help and respond to them from within your SPA."
#
# This project ships no 404.html (do not add one — adding it disables the native
# fallback above and would break every deep link, including /terms and /grievance,
# which are in sitemap.xml).
#
# A catch-all rewrite would be actively harmful here. The Pages redirects
# documentation states that "Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether
# or not an asset matches the incoming request." A `/*` rule would therefore
# shadow real files and serve index.html in place of:
#   robots.txt, sitemap.xml, manifest.json, sw.js, version.json,
#   cache-version.json, /icons/*, /assets/*, and the brand images.
# Those failures are silent — a crawler would receive HTML where it expects XML,
# and the PWA would fail to install.
#
# This file exists only to record that decision so the catch-all is not added
# back without re-reading the above.
